A||||6||jlruiz67||Painting My Fiero for under $1,000??||||1||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||05-13-2001||03:02 PM||||I live in So. California, actually in Laguna Niguel California. Does anyone know where I can get my Med Metallic Red Fiero painted for less than $1,000 and be a good job? I don't want to spend the value of the car on a paint job, but I want a good job done. I have a friend that went to maaco and it look ok at first and after a month the bumper are started to peal from flexing. I don't want a crappy job. Any ideas???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Galen||05-13-2001||03:04 PM||||A paintjob is only as good as the prep done on it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||05-13-2001||03:37 PM||||I just got mine done at Maaco, I did my own prep and got the top end job. I hope it lasts. Looks great right now.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
