Z||000004||maryjane||05-13-2001||09:18 PM||||Had my 84 painted locally  three yrs ago for $600, including prep. They did a pretty good job but found out about halfway through the job they had never done a Fiero. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> Paint has held up good,no oxidation or spiderwebs yet but they got a lot of overspray on rubber parts. You get what you pay for!! I'd go a different route next time.||||reg||9
Z||000005||TheFiero64||05-13-2001||09:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHarry:<BR><B>TheFiero64,<BR>Just wondering, what did Maaco charge you?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>$800<P><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroLisa||05-13-2001||11:02 PM||||Well since prep is a lot of the labor work, if you really want to save money, you can sit in your garage and get it all prepped, and just leave it to them to tape it up and paint it- that will save you the most money. Maaco jobs are mostly bad because the prep work is done in such a short time. It took me about 2 weeks to get my car fully prepped and I would spend about 2-4 hours a day, about 4 days a week on it.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/daytona1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
